.TH DIPICAM378 1 "2026-08-27" "dvbipitools" "dvbipitools Manual"
.SH NAME
dipicam378 \- cs378x (camd35/TCP) key server for CAS testing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dipicam378
.B \-k
.I keyfile
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dipicam378
is a cs378x (camd35/TCP) key server: it holds a device's RSA private key
and answers ECM/EMM requests with a control word. It is a software
smartcard, nothing more.
.PP
The tool speaks the cs378x/camd35 protocol used by oscam-compatible
card readers. It listens on a TCP port, accepts a connection from a
cs378x client such as oscam, and services ECM/EMM requests using a
locally-held PEM-encoded RSA private key for a single device. The
protocol's AES-128 encryption key is derived from the digest of the
configured password, which must match the reader's \fBpassword =\fR
setting.
.PP
.B dipicam378
is for debugging and validation only, pairing with
.BR dipitvhead (1)'s
and
.BR dipiradiohead (1)'s
CAS output so an oscam-driven client can descramble their encrypted
multicast streams as if a real smartcard were present. Built only when
libssl is available; RSA/AES crypto is its sole purpose.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key\ \fI<path>\fR
RSA private key, PEM. Required.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-serial\ \fI<id>\fR
Device's serial, matched against EMM-U addressing. EMM-U for any
other device on the same carousel is skipped. Default: unset, no
filtering.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-port\ \fI<n>\fR
cs378x TCP listen port, the one OSCam's \fBprotocol = cs378x\fR reader
dials into. Default: \fB27500\fR.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-auth\ \fI[user:]<pass>\fR
Password must match the reader's \fBpassword =\fR (default:
\fBdipicam378\fR); its digest is the AES-128 key. If \fIuser\fR is
given, it must match the reader's \fBuser =\fR too, and any other
username is rejected. Omitted: no username check, any connection
accepted.
.TP
.B \-\-caid \fI<hex>\fR
This device's own CAID. ECMs for any other CAID get a CMD08 ("stop
asking"), so OSCam stops re-requesting a CAID this device will never
answer for. Default: unset, no filtering, no CMD08.
.TP
.B \-\-algo \fI<a>\fR
.IR cissa | csa2 .
Selects whether a decrypted ECM's control word is 16 or 8 bytes.
Default: \fBcissa\fR.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Connection accept/close and cs378x message types in/out are logged
unconditionally; this adds ECM/EMM request field detail.
.TP
.B \-\-color \fI<when>\fR
.IR auto | always | never .
Default: \fBauto\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics \fIpath\fR
Unix datagram socket for metrics. Default:
.IR /run/dvbipitools/metrics.sock .
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-id \fIname\fR
Stable instance id. Metrics stay disabled unless this is set.
\fB\-\-metrics\fR and \fB\-\-metrics\-interval\fR require it; either
given without \fB\-\-metrics\-id\fR is a startup error.
.TP
.B \-\-metrics\-interval \fIs\fR
Snapshot interval in seconds. Default: 5.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemonize
Fork to background after startup, detach from terminal.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B dipicam378 \-k device.key \-s cardserial\-01 \-p 27500 \-v \-a someuser:somepassword
Serve a single device's key on the default cs378x port, filtering
EMM-U by serial, verbose logging, username+password auth.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success.
A non-zero status is returned on argument errors or socket failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dipitvhead (1),
.BR dipiradiohead (1),
.BR dipidescramble (1)
.PP
